# Adversarial Probe Set — Coverage Plan

**Target: 63 hand-authored cases minimum** (within brief's 50-100 range; actual count 76 after adding deceptive-image coverage). Every case maps to a specific rule, policy clause, or scenario already defined in `ai_decision_guidelines.md` and the policy corpus — nothing invented fresh.

Field names throughout match the confirmed schema from `gen_returns.py` / `model_pipeline.py`:
`account_age_days, discount_pct, order_value_ratio, seller_return_rate, seller_age_days, seller_customer_frequency, days_since_last_return, order_value, user_avg_order_value, review_count, days_since_delivered, return_to_order_ratio, seller_rating, price, total_orders_at_time, days_left_to_return, image_uploaded, shared_device_flag, category_base_defect, reason_category, total_returns_at_time, phone_verified, category, return_frequency_score, seller_repeat_ratio, weekend_return_ratio, is_prepaid, high_value_return_ratio, returns_last_90d, same_category_return_ratio, return_type, email_verified, returns_last_30d, within_return_window, is_non_returnable, fraud_type, label`

Note: `order_value_ratio` (not `order_value_percentile`) — renamed to match the actual field name after Rushil's fix in `model_pipeline.py`.

